## 11. Interview Questions

**Q1. Why is the array required to be sorted?**

Because duplicates appear next to each other, so we only need to compare adjacent unique values.

**Q2. What is the purpose of pointer `i`?**

It tracks the position of the last unique element.

**Q3. What is the purpose of pointer `j`?**

It traverses the array to find new unique elements.

**Q4. Why do we return `i + 1`?**

Because `i` represents an index, while the answer represents a count.

**Q5. What is the time complexity?**

O(n), because the array is traversed once.

**Q6. What is the space complexity?**

O(1), because no additional data structure is required.

**Q7. Can we use HashSet?**

Yes, but it requires O(n) extra space and does not satisfy the in-place requirement.

**Q8. Can this algorithm work on an unsorted array?**

Not directly. We would need to sort the array first or use a different approach. Sorting would also change the original order.

